1
00:00:02,140 --> 00:00:02,940
Reading

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:07,580
A Student of African Wildlife

3
00:00:09,880 --> 00:00:17,780
It is 5.45 a.m. and the sun is just rising over Gombe National Park in East Africa.

4
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,380
Following Jane’s way of studying chimps,

5
00:00:21,720 --> 00:00:25,160
our group are all going to visit them in the forest.

6
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:32,340
Jane has studied these families of chimps for many years and helped people understand

7
00:00:36,680 --> 00:00:41,920
Watching a family of chimps wake up is our first activity of the day.

8
00:00:42,380 --> 00:00:48,500
This means going back to the place where we left the family sleeping in a tree the night before.

9
00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:55,420
Everybody sits and waits in the shade of the trees while the family begins to wake up

10
00:00:55,420 --> 00:00:56,380
and move off.

11
00:00:57,240 --> 00:01:00,480
Then we follow as they wander into the forest.

12
00:01:01,440 --> 00:01:07,960
Most of the time, chimps either feed or clean each other as a way of showing love in their family.

13
00:01:09,100 --> 00:01:14,360
Jane warns us that our group is going to be very tired and dirty by the afternoon

14
00:01:14,360 --> 00:01:16,280
and she is right.

15
00:01:16,820 --> 00:01:20,000
However, the evening makes it all worthwhile.

16
00:01:21,100 --> 00:01:24,740
We watch the mother chimp and her babies play in the tree.

17
00:01:25,160 --> 00:01:29,060
Then we see them go to sleep together in their nest for the night.

18
00:01:30,300 --> 00:01:36,820
We realize that the bond between members of a chimp family is as strong as in a human family.

19
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:48,160
She spent years observing and recording their daily activities.

20
00:01:49,300 --> 00:01:54,280
Since her childhood she had wanted to work with animals in their own environment.

21
00:01:55,300 --> 00:01:57,780
However, this was not easy.

22
00:01:58,680 --> 00:02:01,980
When she first arrived in Gombe in 1960,

23
00:02:02,520 --> 00:02:05,980
it was unusual for a woman to live in the forest.

24
00:02:14,580 --> 00:02:18,020
Her work changed the way people think about chimps.

25
00:02:18,920 --> 00:02:23,600
For example, one important thing she discovered was that chimps hunt

26
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:25,080
and eat meat.

27
00:02:25,940 --> 00:02:30,580
Until then everyone had thought chimps ate only fruit and nuts.

28
00:02:59,760 --> 00:03:03,640
She has argued that wild animals should be left in the wild

29
00:03:03,640 --> 00:03:07,380
and not used for entertainment or advertisements.

30
00:03:09,200 --> 00:03:13,080
She has helped to set up special places where they can live safely.

31
00:03:13,940 --> 00:03:16,960
She is leading a busy life but she says: "

32
00:03:17,560 --> 00:03:22,580
Once I stop, it all comes crowding in and I remember the chimps in laboratories.

33
00:03:22,980 --> 00:03:23,900
It’s terrible.

34
00:03:24,320 --> 00:03:26,600
It affects me when I watch the wild chimps.

35
00:03:26,980 --> 00:03:29,560
I say to myself, ’Aren’t they lucky?"

36
00:03:30,140 --> 00:03:35,220
And then I think about small chimps in cages though they have done nothing wrong.

37
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:38,640
Once you have seen that you can never forget..."

38
00:03:39,820 --> 00:03:43,060
She has achieved everything she wanted to do:

39
00:03:43,520 --> 00:03:46,000
working with animals in their own environment,

40
00:03:46,540 --> 00:03:52,440
gaining a doctor’s degree and showing that women can live in the forest as men can.

41
00:03:53,100 --> 00:03:57,080
She inspires those who want to cheer the achievements of women.
